# Project Status - Real-time pass (camp/games/reveal) + self-reg notification

Updated: 2026-06-01

- Branch: `realtime-games-reveal-registration` (based on `d7-admin-hub`, so it
  also carries D2–D7 + the family-RBAC parity fix)
- Current completed work: live camping doc + live games/points, synchronized
  winner-reveal countdown, and a self-registration notification-copy fix — a
  quality pass over already-shipped Teams/Games/Registration features.
- Next phase: all TODO phases A–D are ✅; remaining items are the explicit
  D1/D2/D3 deferreds (out of the Android contract).

## Real-time pass (2026-06-01)

- **Live camping doc** (`CampingService.observeCamping(id)` →
  `CampingDetailViewModel`): the shared detail VM (resolved off the
  `CampingDetail` back-stack entry) streams the camping doc, so
  `winnerRevealPolicy` / score-visibility / capacity reach the detail, teams,
  and games screens in real time. Attendees + venue map stay one-shot (loaded on
  first emission); `viewCamping` analytics fires once. Single owned job,
  cancelled in `onCleared`.
- **Live games & points** (`GameService.observeGames`/`observeActivities`):
  `GameViewModel` collects both via `combine` (single owned job per camping,
  cancelled in `onCleared`) instead of one-shot `.get()`. Awarded points/new
  games surface on every device with no reload. Team scores were already live
  via `TeamService.observeTeams`.
- **Synchronized reveal countdown**: `WinnerRevealCeremonyOverlay` anchors on the
  persisted `revealedAt` via `revealCountdownSeconds(revealedAt, now, window=10)`.
  Once an admin reveals, every device streaming the live camping doc converges on
  the same trophy moment (`revealedAt + 10s`); devices opening after the window
  skip straight to the trophy. `TeamsScreen` threads `revealedAt` into the
  overlay; the per-camping "seen" SharedPreferences still prevents replays.
- **Self-registration notification**: `RegistrationNotificationRequest` gained a
  `selfRegistration` flag; self-only → "{requester} registered for {camp}. Review
  and approve." (name once), family registrations keep naming participant(s).
  `CampingRegistrationViewModel` sets the flag when the sole submission is the
  `SelfParticipant`.
- **iOS divergence**: the synced countdown and the self-reg copy differ from
  current iOS (local ceremony; requester+participant copy) per owner request —
  mirror into the iOS repo later so the three platforms don't drift.
- Verification (JBR): `assembleDebug` + `testDebugUnitTest` + `lintDebug` green.
  New: `GameViewModelTest` (live emission), `RegistrationNotificationRequestTest`
  (self/family/multi bodies), `RevealCountdownTest` (anchor math);
  `CampingDetailViewModelTest` still green after the live-stream refactor.
  Single-device only — cross-device sync not verifiable on one local emulator.

