  - Not re-verified on the emulator this session — build-bar only.

## D7 "Admin Hub"

iOS is the source of truth — ported `Features/Admin` (AdminToolsView,
RoleManagementView + ManagedUser/RoleAssignmentService/observer,
AdminOnboardingView + AdminOnboardingStep). Content moderation (C9) and the
report model were already shipped; D7 reuses them.

- **Model** (`data/admin/ManagedUser.kt`): compact directory row (id,
  displayName, email, church, role, photoUrl, updatedAt) decoded **manually**
  from the raw Firestore map (no POJO auto-mapping). `id` falls back
  `id`→`uid`→documentId so docs written before the `id` field still decode.
- **Service** (`data/admin/RoleAssignmentService.kt`): interface + Firestore +
  fake + Hilt binding. `loadUsers(churchFilter)` reads `users` (admins
  unfiltered; non-admin assigners pass their church → `whereEqualTo("church", …)`
  to satisfy the RBAC read rule). `updateRole(uid, role, writeIdField)` writes
  `{role, updatedAt}` via merge-set; **admins** additionally stamp `id == uid`
  (`writeIdField`) for iOS admin-list decoder compatibility — the only
  RBAC-legal place to write `id` (self-profile allowlist + `validChurchRole
  Assignment`'s affectedOnly(role,updatedAt) forbid it everywhere else).
- **Role VM** (`ui/admin/role/RoleManagementViewModel.kt`): sealed
  `RoleManagementUiState` (Loading/Error/Loaded), search + group-by-church
  (alphabetical), local mutation on success, operationMessage/Error. Owns no
  permission logic — the screen passes churchFilter/assignableRoles/writeIdField.
- **Role screen** (`RoleManagementScreen.kt`): Restricted state, scoped-church
  chip, search field, expandable per-church sections, avatar + name/email rows
  with a role `DropdownMenu` (current role checked) gated by
  `canAssignRole(forTargetChurch)`; static role label when not editable.
- **Onboarding VM** (`ui/admin/onboarding/AdminOnboardingViewModel.kt`):
  SharedPreferences-backed completion set (keys mirror the iOS `@AppStorage`
  flags); markComplete / toggle / reset.
- **Onboarding screen** (`AdminOnboardingScreen.kt`): progress ring (Canvas
  arc) + gradient bar, 5 step cards. Camping/announcement steps mark-complete
  then navigate (CampingCreate / AnnouncementComposer); roles/rules/
  notifications are manual toggles (mirrors iOS — those are console/infra
  tasks). Reset button.
- **Hub** (`ui/admin/AdminToolsScreen.kt`): expanded from the C9 stub into
  Operations (Setup Guide if admin-tools · Registration Review · Role
  Assignment if any-role-assigner) + Moderation (Content Reports + pending
  badge) + Infrastructure (Security Rules / Firestore Backup / Notification
  Dispatch info rows + footer). Restricted unless moderator OR admin-tools OR
  any-role-assigner.
- **Navigation**: typed routes `AppRoute.RoleManagement`
  (`profile/admin/roles`) + `AppRoute.AdminOnboarding`
  (`profile/admin/onboarding`); hub callbacks thread to RoleManagement /
  AdminOnboarding / RegistrationReview.
- **i18n**: admin-hub, role-management, and onboarding strings added to EN, FR,
  PT-BR.

## Notes / deviations

- **`id` field**: neither shipped iOS nor the existing Android profile-save
  writes `id`; the field is supplied in production by the web app / seed. The
  iOS `ManagedUser` decoder decodes a non-optional `id` (no `@DocumentID`), so
  Android stamps `id` on the admin role-update — the maximum the RBAC allows —
  to avoid regressing the shared admin list. Android's own list never needs it
  (it falls back to the document id).
- **Role assignment in-app**: unlike iOS (which defers leadership grants to the
  Firebase console), the Android hub assigns roles in-app — admins can grant any
  role, church-scoped youth_director/pastor only guest/user/adult, exactly per
  the deployed `validChurchRoleAssignment` rule. The onboarding "Assign
  leadership roles" step is still a manual toggle to mirror the iOS checklist.
- Implemented under `ui/admin/role/` + `ui/admin/onboarding/` + `data/admin/`.

